  "summary": "Rivets, oil and dusk — the interwar machine future, armored and grainy.",
  "description": "Dieselpunk is the retrofuture of the interwar years: riveted dreadnought geometry, airship hangars, testbed monoplanes, streamliner locomotives, art-deco radios and the somber industrial palette of oil, steel and smoke. The term — coined online in 2001 (Lewis Pollak & Dan LaSoura, for the RPG Children of the Sun) — sets the tone against steampunk's brass: diesel is grimmer, heavier, film-grainier. Games (Crimson Skies, Iron Harvest, Bioshock's rapture-era machines), cosplay and model-making sustain the aesthetic, and its art direction leans on Weimar posters, WPA murals and RKO serial menace.",
  "culturalContext": "Dieselpunk is the interwar machine future — riveted dreadnoughts, airship hangars, streamliners and oil-and-steel palettes — coined in 2001 as steampunk's grim industrial sibling. Games (Crimson Skies, Iron Harvest), cosplay and Weimar-WPA poster aesthetics sustain its heavy-metal retrofuture.",
